g materials and extra safety setup. Those costs are real and should appear in a repair estimate, but they are frequently left out."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"My Over-the-Rhine rowhouse shares a wall with the neighbor. How is shared damage handled?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each owner’s policy generally covers its own building, and shared elements like party walls or connected roofs can require coordination between two insurers. Clear photos and a scope that shows where damage begins and ends on each side help keep that process moving."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is water coming through my hillside basement wall covered?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the cause. Many policies exclude surface water, groundwater and earth movement, while covering sudden water from plumbing or, with an endorsement, drain backup. Check your policy and document the source carefully."}}],"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cincinnati-ohio/#faq"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance appraisal in Cincinnati, Ohio","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Need an insurance appraiser in Cincinnati, Ohio? We review hail, wind and water estimates on hillside homes and rowhouses across Hamilton County.","provider":{"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Cincinnati","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Ohio"}},"url":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cincinnati-ohio/","@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cincinnati-ohio/#service"}]}</script>
